Read TASK.md and AGENTS.md. Work test-first, in two stages.

Stage 1, the tests: write test/rooms/core_test.clj, clojure.test tests for rooms.core, and test/slots/core_test.clj, clojure.test tests for slots.core. Together they must capture everything TASK.md says -- every rule, boundary and tie-break, when ranges clash, who may cancel, how the earliest slot is chosen, and what book-all returns -- so that an implementation that gets any of them wrong fails a test. Write as many tests as that takes. Commit the tests with git (message 'tests') before writing any implementation.

Stage 2, the implementation: write src/rooms/core.clj and src/slots/core.clj and run bin/test until it exits 0. Treat your tests as the contract: if a test fails, fix the implementation; change a test only when it is genuinely wrong about TASK.md, never just to make it pass, and say in your summary each change you made to a test and why.

When done, write NOTES.md: what was hard to pin down in tests, and anything you could not express.
